  },
  "notes": "Paul Vaurie’s exact 2024 public-domain Qualla photograph establishes the standing limewashed sandstone, green-black sash, dark gable and green copper lantern. The National Park Service identifies the east access stairs, spiral tower section, lens height and reconstructed cottage."
